Note = {International Workshop on Diffuse Pollution-Management Measures and
   Control Technique, Anhui Univ Sci \& Technol, Huainan, PEOPLES R CHINA,
   OCT 27-29, 2010},
Abstract = {The content of eight heavy metals (Hg, As, Cd, Cr, Cu, Zn, Pb, Ni) in
   fly ash (FA) were determined through agitation leaching test, the
   dissolution characteristic of them were also analyzed. The results
   showed that the content of eight heavy metals was as follows: Ni > Cr >
   Cu > Pb > Zn > As > Cd > Hg.In the leaching test, the leaching content
   of eight heavy metals in sequence was:Pb > Ni > Cu > Zn > Cr > AS > Cd >
   Hg, and the leaching simplicity of them was: Hg > Cd > Pb > As > Zn > Ni
   > Cu > Cr.On basis of the total amount analysis and leaching
   characteristics, the safety of FA as filler material in wastewater
   treatment was evaluated comprehensively and systematically,and then
   pollution prevention measures was proposed according to the feature of
   the FA used in wastewater treatment},
