Abstract = {The new sustainable health system named bio-toilet is an important
   subsystem of the Onsite Wastewater Differentiable Treatment System for
   treating the toilet wastes using sawdust as matrix. In this study the
   changes of physical and chemical natures of dry matter (DM), ash, bulk
   density and porosity of the matrix were studied with the composting
   under continuous feed operation conditions in a range of moisture
   content (50\%-60\%) and temperature (50-60 degrees C), and the free air
   space (FAS) as an index was used to evaluate the venting quality of the
   bulk-matrix. As a result, the content of TS and ash increased
   continuously in the reactor with composting lead to the increased of
   bulk density, however, lead to the value of porosity and FAS of matrix
   decreased, the decreasing of FAS would has a directly influence on the
   microbial growth. Microbial growth rate coefficient k was the function
   of the value of FAS, the value of k>0 when the value of FAS>0.622, the
   aerobic microorganisms was proliferation; and the value of k<0 when the
   value of FAS<0.622, the aerobic microorganisms was negative growth; the
   value of FAS =0.622 is in the critical condition of the aerobic
   condition in the reactor.},
