Note = {Asia-Pacific Conference on Mind Brain and Education, Washington, DC, OCT
   25-27, 2008},
Organization = {Int Soc Mind, Brain \& Educ; SE Univ, Key Lab Child Dev \& Learning Sci;
   Thinktank - Handsbrain Educ; SE Univ State Key Lab Bioelect; Chinese Soc
   Biomed Elect},
Abstract = {. The attentional capture effect of emotional faces in sufficient or
   restricted attentional conditions were investigated In a modified visual
   search paradigm, three kinds of schematic faces (angry, happy, and
   neutral face) were included as the stimuli. Participants ought to search
   for a target face having a dot and respond the dot position. The results
   of Experiment I showed that only angry face as the target can facilitate
   response compared to the control. And angry face as distractor can slow
   down the response. Experiment 2 included inverted faces for decreasing
   emotional content and found the effect of inverted angry face was not
   the same as the upright condition. When attention was cued to a specific
   location in experiment 3, the effect of angry faces outside the attended
   area became weaker. In conclusion, the results support that angry face
   can capture attention automatically but require attentional resources.},
