Note = {International Conference on Water Resource and Environmental Protection
   (WREP), Hong Kong, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 07-08, 2014},
Abstract = {As the convergence regulation and storage hub of the large-scale
   inter-basin water transfer project-the ``Yellow River-to-Tianjin Water
   Diversion Project{''} and the ``North-to-South Water Diversion
   Project{''}, Lake Hengshui has high ecological value, economic value and
   social value. We found the quality of water in Lake Hengshui belongs to
   an alkaline and type of sodium chloride group II water. Using the
   comprehensive index method, we prove the Lake Hengshui is in a state of
   mesotrophication or eutrophication. The study of sedimentary diatoms
   combination indicated that Achnanthes minutissima, Cymbella
   microcephala, Navicula cryptotenella and Stephanodiscus minitulus is the
   main species in Lake Hengshui. The dominant species is Achnanthes
   minutissima (20.90\%) and Cymbella microcephala (18.83\%), and they
   vividly indicate the tropic status of mesotrophication and
   eutrophication in Lake Hengshui.},
