   Marrakesh, MOROCCO, SEP 19-24, 2004},
Organization = {Int Water Assoc; AMEPA; ONEP; LYDEC},
Abstract = {Municipal leachate was treated in an experimental unit of constructed
   wetlands of subsurface flow type. The parameters studied were organics
   (BOD and COD), solids and heavy metals (Zn, Ni, Cu, Cr and Pb). Using
   two types of emergent plants of Scirpus globulosus and Eriocaulon
   sexangulare, more than 80\% removal was achieved for all the parameters.
   E sexangulare removed organics and heavy metals better than Scirpus
   globulosus. A higher concentration of heavy metals in the influent did
   not change the removal efficiency.},
