Abstract = {This paper describes several techniques and methods for sludge
   characterization which are recently developed and used in our ongoing
   research on biological phosphorus removal (BPR): (i) chemical
   measurement of the poly-hydroxy-alkanoate (PHA) content of the biomass,
   (ii) bioassay for glycogen determination in BPR systems, (iii)
   determination of the fraction of denitrifying phosphorus accumulating
   organisms (DPAOs) in P-removing sludge, (iv) determination of the
   aerobic and anoxic ATP/NADH(2) ratio (delta value) in BPR systems, and
   (v) determination of the glycogen accumulating organisms
   (GAOs)/phosphorus accumulating organisms (PAOs) ratio in activated
   sludge. (C) 1999 Published by Elsevier Science Ltd on Behalf of the
