   Management},
Abstract = {Utilizing industrial ecosystem theory, this paper analyzed the
   competition, mutualism and up-down stream relationship among enterprises
   in industrial clusters. It was found that the precondition for the
   perfect development of an industrial cluster is that the competitive
   members must be different and the mutualism members must be competitive.
   It was also found that the conditions of an industrial cluster to keep
   ecological equilibrium are that enterprises in the cluster must differ
   in products and technologies, form cooperative networks and keep
   frequent communication with the external world.},
