   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {Different recycle channels and product features always lead to different
   economic and environmental effects for end-of-life products. For an
   enterprise, the top priority is to find whether the recycle of
   end-of-life products will make positive economic effects, which are the
   prerequisite of its remanufacture behavior. And then it will choose the
   most efficient recycling system of end-of-life products to optimize its
   profit. As for government, it need to know the comprehensive effects of
   different end-of-life products and different recycling channels to make
   out proper policy which could encourage enterprises' recycling and
   remanufacturing behaviors. This paper utilizes the method of
   input-and-output to calculate economic and environmental effects of
   remanufacturing end-of-life products respectively, and finally induce
   its comprehensive effects. Through our research, we conclude that
   recycle-and-remanufacture end-of-life products could be categorized into
   four types and government could accordingly take different policies to
   encourage them.},
