   Management},
Abstract = {Global value chain (GVC) theory shows the spatial distribution of the
   value chain, and the global distribution of auto industry's value chain
   constitutes a global automobile industry value chain. Chinese automobile
   industry is at the low value-added segment of the GVC. Small-scale, low
   degree of specialization and R\&D capacity and lack of independent
   brands have also restricted the upgrading of Chinese automobile
   industry. The article expounds the theory of global value chain and the
   structure of automobile industry value chain. Then it analyzes the
   problems of Chinese automobile industry and points out the adverse
   factors for industrial upgrading. And then the article analyzes the
   paths of upgrading for Chinese auto industry and finally provides some
   advices to promote its development.},
