   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {In this paper, the scale and efficiency of China's auto industry
   relationships are analyzed through two dimensions of space and time.
   First, a group of comprehensive index system is established to reflect
   the current scale and efficiency of auto industry of Chinese provinces
   and cities, and the features of the spatial distribution about the scale
   and efficiency of China's auto industry are analyzed by hierarchical
   clustering method. Then we calculated the time distribution of
   two-dimensional indicators about scale and efficiency of China's auto
   industry by two indicators of the productivity of the overall labor from
   the year 2000 to 2006 and return on assets analysis, and found that
   there is an obvious staged representation of the size and efficiency in
   auto industry. Ladder-shaped features are found about China's auto
   industry development by the integrated dynamics on the two dimensions of
   scale and efficiency in space and time. Finally, through comparisons
   with advanced countries of the concentration degree in auto industry, we
   come to the conclusion that China's auto industry can obtain trade
   interests by its agglomeration advantages to enhance the status of the
   international division of labor in the auto industry.},
