   Management},
Abstract = {Based on the data from the fifth national sample survey of population
   census, the statistical yearbooks of kuerle and another 8 counties from
   1998 to 2006, and many data about all the,towns in 2006, this article
   studies the correlation between the population of ethnic minorities and
   the urbanization with the help of the statistical software SPSS13.0. The
   following are the conclusions. Firstly, the contribution rate to the
   level of urbanization is proportional to the amount of the population of
   one ethnic minority. Secondly, the more dispersivity of population
   distribution of one ethnic minority has a higher level of urbanization.
   Thirdly, a town with the less Pm! dation proportion of ethnic minorities
   has a higher level of urbanization. Fourthly, the development of the
   tertiary industry strongly influences the urbanization level of the
   ethnic minorities' population. Therefore, the author gives three
   strategies of improving the urbanization level of the ethnic minorities'
   population. That is to enhance the introjections between the national
   culture and common culture in the ethnic regions to effectively improve
   the level of urbanization of the ethnic minorities, vigorously develop
   the industries with the ethnic characteristics in ethnic minority areas
   to improve the development level of tertiary industry and strengthen the
   population migration of ethnic nationalities to increase areas inhabited
   by many ethnic groups.},
