   Management},
Abstract = {For a transitional society, poverty roots in a series of institutions
   which caused poverty. The institutions together with other factors such
   as education (human capital), investment, and consumption interact and
   develop into an accumulating and circulating linkage mechanism in which
   individual peasant without proper living ability and rights is easily
   trapped into the status of poverty. Furthermore, social transformation
   greatly changed the original industry, employment structure, and even
   mode of production and life style, then people who are accustomed to the
   traditional society can not adapt well to the society after
   transformation. Thus they evolved into a Marx's relative and absolute
   prole. To break the poverty lock-in, one feasible policy options is to
   rebuild cooperative economy base on farmland contract, improve the rural
   infrastructure, develop rural finance and construct effective social
   security system, transform traditional agriculture into modern
   agriculture and develop more non-agriculture industry inside
   agriculture.},
