   Management},
Abstract = {Motor vehicles are one of the main causes of environmental pollution. In
   recent years, the civilian car ownership in China is increasing rapidly,
   but it has different development trend between the 31 provinces of
   china. This article uses the Gompertz model and panel data model to
   forecast the national and provincial civilian car ownership to the year
   2020. The results show that: Gompertz model fits well the development
   trend of civilian car ownership of all the provinces; According to the
   respective average growth rate of per capita GDP and population between
   1998 and 2007, most of the provinces will get the turning points in the
   year 2015-2020; Using exponential smoothing method to predict the future
   population and GDP, the model predicts that the national car ownership
   will exceed 160 million by 2015 and it will reach 260 million in 2020.},
