   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {Elastoplastic models can not explain accumulation of deformation and
   bearing capacity decrease caused by neglecting of the damage evolution
   in ductile material, thus the stress distribution used to higher than
   the structure actual bearing capacity. Simplified elastoplastic damage
   model stress-strain curves are derived from specifications, which suit
   to finite element software ABAQUS. Pure bending simply supported beam is
   used to prove the simplified curves correctness, then the simplified
   elastoplastic damage model is applied to ShenXigou hydropower station
   prestressed pier nonlinear finite element analysis. The results are
   compared with linear elastic and contact nonlinear calculation result.
   The results show that, the elastoplastic damage model better reflects
   the real stress distribution characteristics than linear elastic
   analysis. Consider the contact nonlinear of prestressed pier and steel
   anchor block will have a more realistic simulation of cracks. The
   results are significant to guidance the layout of prestressed
   reinforcement and prestressed pier design.},
