   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {Biofuels are an important tool in the fight global warming. Bioethanol
   is only one part of a many-faceted solution to the problem of global
   warming. Concerns about accelerating rates of atmospheric carbon dioxide
   concentration increase and the resulting impacts on global warming are
   motivating efforts to develop a renewable fuel like bioethanol. The use
   of lignocellulosic wastes as feedstock offers good perspectives for
   large scale production of fuel ethanol at competitive cost. The
   unutilized lignocellulosic raw material like weeds and forest waste
   could efficiently be converted into bioethanol by different processing
   steps to yield maximum monomer sugars. The conversion of foody raw
   material into ethanol will not be economical viable and there is a
   danger of war between food and fuel in future. The main environmental
   advantage of fuel ethanol is its sustainability in using a renewable
   resource as a feedstock, thus promoting independence of fossil fuel, and
   maintaining the level of green house gas (CO2). Combustion of these
   fuels produces CO2 gas which would be assimilated through photosynthesis
   and metabolized to a building block of plants. In total, almost no net
   CO2 is produces by using fuels generated from lignocellulosic biomass.
   Therefore lignocellulosic derived ethanol could be used as an
   environmentally friendly liquid fuel. Current paper describes the
   laboratory research and basic role of bioethanol from lignocellulosic
   wastes in Indian scenario in global climate change.},
